<title>SWEDEN: SWIMMING-POLL BREAKS WOMEN'S 200 FREESTYLE WORLD RECORD.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-POLL BREAKS WOMEN'S 200 FREESTYLE WORLD RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>GOTHENBURG, Sweden 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Claudia Poll of Costa Rica broke her own world short-course women's 200 metres freestyle record at the world short-course swimming championships on Friday.</p>
<p>Poll clocked one minute 54.17 seconds to beat the mark of 1:55.42 she set at the last world short-course championships in Rio de Janeiro on December 1, 1995.</p>
